      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A shared solvothermal protocol was used for 1 and 2. Ln(NO3)3·6H2O, H3L (2-(2,3-dihydroxypropyliminomethyl)-6-methoxyphenol), pivalic acid, and Et3N in a 5:5:30:2 molar ratio were reacted in MeOH/CH3CN (1:1) in a Teflon-lined autoclave at 80 °C for 5 days, affording yellow crystals. H3L was prepared by reported procedures and is also formed in situ by condensation of 2-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde (L1) with 3-amino-1,2-propanediol (L2).",
