      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Hexanuclear Gd cluster 1 shows weak antiferromagnetic Gd···Gd coupling and a large magnetocaloric effect. χmT at 300 K is 47.43 cm3 K mol−1 (calc. 47.25 for six uncoupled Gd3+), falling to 21.64 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Curie–Weiss fit (T > 150 K) gives C = 48.10 cm3 K mol−1 and θ = −4.45 K. Magnetization reaches 39.1 Nβ at 5 T and 2.0 K. −ΔSm = 20.0 J kg−1 K−1 at 4 K for ΔH = 5 T (abstract/MCE discussion also quotes 19.58–20.0 J kg−1 K−1).",
        "measurements": [
